            <ArticleTitle>The role of oxidative stress in influenza virus infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>580-586</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1286-4579(17)30123-5</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.micinf.2017.08.008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Virus-induced oxidative stress plays an important role in the regulation of the host immune system. In this review, we provide backgrounds of the pathogenic mechanism of oxidative stress induced by influenza virus and the specific oxidant-sensitive pathways, and highlight that antioxidant is one of the effective strategies against influenza virus infection.</AbstractText>
